WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:05.955
Mrs. Errol seemed flustered when Mr. Havisham and Cedric arrived.

2
00:00:05.956 --> 00:00:11.912
"I'm sorry, Mr. Havisham," she said, "but I must speak to my servant.

3
00:00:11.913 --> 00:00:15.090
Mary has just received some terrible news."

4
00:00:15.091 --> 00:00:22.340
Mrs. Errol hurried into the kitchen, leaving Cedric to entertain the lawyer.

5
00:00:22.341 --> 00:00:27.677
Mr. Havisham sat in a chair while Cedric took a seat opposite him.

6
00:00:27.678 --> 00:00:33.968
Mr. Havisham wasn't used to talking to children and had no idea what to say.

7
00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:40.576
Cedric finally broke the silence. "I don't really understand what an earl is.

8
00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:44.810
And when a boy is going to be one, he ought to know."

9
00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:50.330
Mr. Havisham was relieved. This was a topic he could talk about.

10
00:00:50.331 --> 00:00:55.164
"Earls are important men," the lawyer began.

11
00:00:55.165 --> 00:00:59.300
"Over the centuries they've helped to govern England.

12
00:00:59.301 --> 00:01:03.896
They usually come from very old families and—"

13
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.356
Cedric popped up from the sofa with excitement.

14
00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:14.466
"The woman who sells apples is very old! She must be close to a hundred!"

15
00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:20.916
"Well . . . an old person is not the same as an old family

16
00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:28.777
. The first Earl of Dorincourt received his title almost four hundred years

17
00:01:28.778 --> 00:01:34.238
ago." "Oh, I see." Cedric sat

18
00:01:34.239 --> 00:01:42.339
down. They fell into silence again. Mr. Havisham studied a crack in the

19
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:49.573
wall. Cedric sighed. "Sometimes I wish I had lots of

20
00:01:49.574 --> 00:01:55.577
money." Mr. Havisham raised his eyebrows. "What would you do with

21
00:01:55.578 --> 00:02:02.421
it?" "I'd buy the apple seller a tent for her stall and a stove and a warm

22
00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:08.055
shawl. She's so poor that she has to work every day, even when it's

23
00:02:08.056 --> 00:02:16.293
raining." Cedric stopped to think. "And on rainy days, I'd give her a dollar so she could stay

24
00:02:16.294 --> 00:02:22.913
home!" Mr. Havisham smiled at his generosity. "Why would you do all

25
00:02:22.914 --> 00:02:27.154
that?" "Because she's been kind to me," Cedric

26
00:02:27.155 --> 00:02:34.073
explained. "When I fell and cut my knee, she gave me an apple for

27
00:02:34.074 --> 00:02:38.684
free." "That was kind," Mr. Havisham

28
00:02:38.685 --> 00:02:45.383
agreed. He suddenly found himself enjoying this conversation. "What else would you

29
00:02:45.384 --> 00:02:47.963
do?" "I'd like to help my friend

30
00:02:47.964 --> 00:02:53.965
Dick. He's just a few years older than I am, but he has a shoeshine stand with a

31
00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:58.658
partner. Once I had a new ball that bounced into the

32
00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:05.639
street. Dick ran after it and brought it back. We've been friends ever

33
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.257
since." Cedric frowned. "The shoeshine business isn't too good right

34
00:03:11.258 --> 00:03:20.901
now." Mr. Havisham forced himself not to smile at Cedric's knowledge of the shoeshine business. "And why is that?"

35
00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:26.514
"Well, everybody likes Dick, but nobody likes his partner.

36
00:03:26.515 --> 00:03:34.735
Jake's a bad guy. I wish Dick could have his own shoeshine stand."

37
00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:42.425
Mr. Havisham leaned forward. "What about you? Is there anything you want?"

38
00:03:42.426 --> 00:03:52.987
Cedric grinned. "A pony! Sometimes when Mama and I are walking, we see a boy riding. I'd like to ride!"

39
00:03:52.988 --> 00:03:57.497
Just then Mrs. Errol came into the parlor, looking upset.

40
00:03:57.498 --> 00:04:02.358
"Mary's husband is sick, and now he's lost his job."

41
00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:08.490
"I must talk to her!" Cedric slipped from the sofa and left the room.

42
00:04:08.491 --> 00:04:13.913
"That's quite a boy you have," Mr. Havisham said to Mrs. Errol.

43
00:04:13.914 --> 00:04:21.729
"There will be many changes in his life. One day he'll have lots of power—"

44
00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.496
"Oh, he's just a little boy!

45
00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:31.600
I hope I can teach him to use his power wisely." Mrs. Errol seemed distressed.

46
00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:36.888
"Cedric will have lots of money too," Mr. Havisham went on.

47
00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:40.567
"The earl wants me to buy whatever he wants.

48
00:04:40.568 --> 00:04:49.207
But Cedric only wants to help others. I don't think that's what the earl had in mind."

49
00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:56.620
Mrs. Errol gave a sympathetic sigh. "That poor, lonely man.

50
00:04:56.621 --> 00:05:02.415
His sons have died, and now he just wants to be kind to my boy."

51
00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:09.345
Mr. Havisham couldn't look her in the eye. The earl was far different from what she imagined.

52
00:05:09.346 --> 00:05:13.853
The earl's motive was to ensure that Cedric would come to England.

53
00:05:13.854 --> 00:05:20.286
"Give my grandson whatever he wants," the earl had told Mr. Havisham.

54
00:05:20.287 --> 00:05:30.899
"I don't care what you spend. Make sure he has money in his pocket and knows it came from me."

55
00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.354
Cedric walked slowly back into the parlor.

56
00:05:34.355 --> 00:05:39.534
"Mary doesn't know how they'll pay the rent," he said sadly.

57
00:05:39.535 --> 00:05:46.293
"Their landlord is threatening to evict them. I wish we could help them."

58
00:05:46.294 --> 00:05:49.139
Mr. Havisham made a quick decision.

59
00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.399
He reached into his pocket and handed some money to Cedric.

60
00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:58.634
"I'm sure the earl would want Mary to have this."

61
00:05:58.635 --> 00:06:06.179
"Twenty-five dollars!" Cedric's eyes widened in amazement.

62
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:10.219
"That's a fortune!" Mrs. Errol said.

63
00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:19.061
Running toward the kitchen, Cedric called out, "Mary! Look what I have for you from my grandfather!"

64
00:06:19.062 --> 00:06:24.086
He returned a few minutes later, a big smile on his face.

65
00:06:24.087 --> 00:06:29.879
"I never saw anybody cry with joy like Mary just did," Cedric said.

66
00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:36.896
"Maybe being an earl won't be so bad after all!"

